WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A market claim travels. Does its evidence? Keep the source, the observation and the limits in the same record.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:17.000
A price leaves out resolution rules. A progress bar does not prove migration. Missing context follows the claim into a report.

3
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Sourcebrief is a solo project by EazyHood, built with extensive OpenAI Codex assistance to make research briefs easier to check.

4
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Inspect the source. Save a checkpoint. Compare a later observation. Export a dated brief, without losing the original evidence.

5
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Panta supplies the catalogue and market details: resolution wording, source identifiers, indicated prices and missing information.

6
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Solami reads the DBC pool, configuration, both token mints and Clock together on mainnet. The brief keeps their shared context slot and account hashes.

7
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:06.000
An actual application capture, shown at native resolution as a static illustration. The separate demonstration shows application use.

8
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Meteora’s official SDK interprets curves, fees and migration. It calculates a local scenario where supported. No wallet, signature or executed transaction.

9
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:28.000
For migrated pools or external transfer hooks, the calculator explains why it abstains instead of inventing an output.

10
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Two evidence types, one editorial workflow. No invented link between an event and a token. Export observations, calculations and limits.

11
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:48.000
No measured external traction or revenue yet. Next: an opt-in reviewer pilot. A shared team workspace is proposed, not built.

12
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Sourcebrief. Market claims change. Keep the evidence. Explore the open-source code and the live research desk.
